KLEE's RPATH already covers `/usr/local/lib` and `/usr/lib/llvm-16/lib`, and I also added `/etc/ld.so.conf.d/usr-local.conf` + `ldconfig` so `libstp`/`libminisat` resolve without extra env vars.

## Environment in `~/.bashrc`

Ubuntu's `.bashrc` returns early for non-interactive shells (`[ -z "$PS1" ] && return` at line 8), which would have skipped any exports appended at the bottom when a test does `source ~/.bashrc`. So the block is placed **above** that early return, and it is idempotent:

```bash
case ":$PATH:" in *:/usr/local/bin:*) ;; *) export PATH="/usr/local/bin:$PATH" ;; esac
case ":$CPATH:" in *:/usr/local/include:*) ;; *) export CPATH="/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:$CPATH}" ;; esac
case ":$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:" in *:/usr/local/lib:*) ;; *) export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}" ;; esac
```

`CPATH=/usr/local/include` makes `#include <klee/klee.h>` resolvable with no `-I` flag (header installed at `/usr/local/include/klee/klee.h`).

## Verification (run from `bash -c 'source ~/.bashrc; ...'`)

- `command -v klee` → `/usr/local/bin/klee`; `klee --version` → `KLEE 3.1`, `Build mode: Release (Asserts: ON)`, `Ubuntu LLVM version 16.0.6`
- Compiled a test program with plain `clang-16 -emit-llvm -c -g -O0` (no `-I`) — header resolved purely via `CPATH`
- `klee add.bc` → `KLEE: Using STP solver backend`, `SAT solver: MiniSat`, symbolic `a+b == 7` assertion found, 2 `.ktest` files generated (STP is the default backend, no flag needed)
- No uClibc present anywhere; `POSIX runtime disabled`, `klee-uclibc runtime` copy skipped

Sources/build trees remain in `/tmp/{minisat,stp,klee}{,-build}` (~70 MB) in case you want to rebuild or run KLEE's own test suites.
